</div><div class="jp-RenderedHTMLCommon jp-RenderedMarkdown jp-MarkdownOutput" data-mime-type="text/markdown">
<h2 id="Conclusion">Conclusion<a class="anchor-link" href="#Conclusion">¶</a></h2><p>In this project, a Sales Prediction model was developed using advertising
spending on TV, Radio, and Newspaper.</p>
<p>Exploratory Data Analysis showed that advertising expenditure has a
relationship with product sales, with TV advertising generally showing the
strongest relationship.</p>
<p>Two regression models were trained:</p>
<ol>
<li>Linear Regression</li>
<li>Random Forest Regressor</li>
</ol>
<p>The models were evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE), Root Mean
Squared Error (RMSE), and R² Score.</p>
<p>The model with the lower MAE and RMSE and higher R² score was selected as
the best-performing model.</p>
<p>Feature importance/coefficient analysis was used to determine which
advertising channel has the greatest impact on sales.</p>
<p>The residual plot was also analyzed to check whether the prediction errors
were randomly distributed around zero.</p>
<p>Overall, the project demonstrates how machine learning can be used to
predict product sales based on advertising expenditure across different
media channels.</p>
</div>
